      <h1 data-en="How Much Does Booking Software Cost for Barbershops in 2026?" data-fr="Combien coûte un logiciel de réservation pour barbershops en 2026?">How Much Does Booking Software Cost for Barbershops in 2026?</h1>
      <div class="article-meta" data-en="Published June 14, 2026 · 8 min read" data-fr="Publié le 14 juin 2026 · 8 min de lecture">Published June 14, 2026 · 8 min read</div>
    </div>

    <div class="article-body">
      <p data-en="Picking booking software for your barbershop isn't just about finding the lowest sticker price. A platform advertised at $0/month can cost you more than one charging $30/month — depending on how many new clients you take and whether the platform skims a commission from every booking." data-fr="Choisir un logiciel de réservation pour votre barbershop ne se résume pas à trouver le prix affiché le plus bas. Une plateforme annoncée à 0$/mois peut vous coûter plus qu'une facturant 30$/mois — selon le nombre de nouveaux clients que vous accueillez et si la plateforme prélève une commission sur chaque réservation.">Picking booking software for your barbershop isn't just about finding the lowest sticker price. A platform advertised at $0/month can cost you more than one charging $30/month — depending on how many new clients you take and whether the platform skims a commission from every booking.</p>

      <p data-en="This guide breaks down how each major platform is actually priced in 2026, what hidden fees exist, and what a realistic annual cost looks like for a two-barber shop doing 20 new clients per month at $50 average. No sales pitch — just the numbers." data-fr="Ce guide décompose comment chaque plateforme majeure est réellement tarifée en 2026, quels frais cachés existent, et à quoi ressemble un coût annuel réaliste pour un barbershop à deux barbiers effectuant 20 nouveaux clients par mois à 50$ en moyenne. Pas d'argumentaire de vente — juste les chiffres.">This guide breaks down how each major platform is actually priced in 2026, what hidden fees exist, and what a realistic annual cost looks like for a two-barber shop doing 20 new clients per month at $50 average. No sales pitch — just the numbers.</p>

      <h2 data-en="The Four Pricing Models You'll Encounter" data-fr="Les quatre modèles de tarification que vous rencontrerez">The Four Pricing Models You'll Encounter</h2>

      <p data-en="Before comparing platforms, understand that booking software uses four distinct pricing structures — and the model matters as much as the number:" data-fr="Avant de comparer les plateformes, sachez que les logiciels de réservation utilisent quatre structures de tarification distinctes — et le modèle compte autant que le chiffre :">Before comparing platforms, understand that booking software uses four distinct pricing structures — and the model matters as much as the number:</p>

      <ul>
        <li data-en="Monthly subscription — A flat fee every month regardless of appointment volume. Predictable and easy to budget. Examples: Booksy ($29.99), Bookwize ($19), Vagaro ($30+), GlossGenius ($24), Acuity ($20)." data-fr="Abonnement mensuel — Un forfait fixe chaque mois, peu importe le volume de rendez-vous. Prévisible et facile à budgéter. Exemples : Booksy (29,99$), Bookwize (19$), Vagaro (30$+), GlossGenius (24$), Acuity (20$)."><strong>Monthly subscription</strong> — A flat fee every month regardless of appointment volume. Predictable and easy to budget. Examples: Booksy ($29.99), Bookwize ($19), Vagaro ($30+), GlossGenius ($24), Acuity ($20).</li>
        <li data-en="Commission-based — No monthly fee, but the platform takes a percentage cut of revenue from certain bookings. Feels free up front; scales with your revenue. Example: Fresha (20% on new-client bookings)." data-fr="Basé sur les commissions — Pas de frais mensuel, mais la plateforme prend un pourcentage des revenus de certaines réservations. Semble gratuit au départ ; évolue avec vos revenus. Exemple : Fresha (20% sur les réservations de nouveaux clients)."><strong>Commission-based</strong> — No monthly fee, but the platform takes a percentage cut of revenue from certain bookings. Feels free up front; scales with your revenue. Example: Fresha (20% on new-client bookings).</li>
        <li data-en="One-time payment — A single fee that grants permanent access. No recurring costs. Rare in the market. Example: Bookwize ($299 lifetime)." data-fr="Paiement unique — Un seul paiement qui accorde un accès permanent. Pas de frais récurrents. Rare sur le marché. Exemple : Bookwize (299$ à vie)."><strong>One-time payment</strong> — A single fee that grants permanent access. No recurring costs. Rare in the market. Example: Bookwize ($299 lifetime).</li>
        <li data-en="Freemium — A genuinely free tier with limited capacity, plus paid upgrades for more staff or features. Example: Square Appointments (free for 1 staff, $29/mo for 2–5 staff)." data-fr="Freemium — Un niveau vraiment gratuit avec une capacité limitée, plus des mises à niveau payantes pour plus d'employés ou de fonctionnalités. Exemple : Square Appointments (gratuit pour 1 employé, 29$/mois pour 2–5 employés)."><strong>Freemium</strong> — A genuinely free tier with limited capacity, plus paid upgrades for more staff or features. Example: Square Appointments (free for 1 staff, $29/mo for 2–5 staff).</li>
      </ul>

